# Data conversion between byte and terabyte

Verifies direct data conversion between byte and terabyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1B to 0.0000TB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5B yields 0.0000TB; backward, converting 1TB to 1000000000000B preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5TB yields 1500000000000.0B. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1B
print(forward_whole->to(TB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5B
print(forward_fractional->to(TB))
backward_whole: int = 1TB
print(backward_whole->to(B))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5TB
print(backward_fractional->to(B))

<<< stdout
0.0000TB
0.0000TB
1000000000000B
1500000000000.0B

<<< stderr
